{{/*
  The licences page. The components and their licences are not written here:
  they are each piece's THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, rendered, so the page says
  what the releases carry and cannot say anything else. main.go says where
  each copy comes from.
*/}}
{{template "head" .}}
</head>
<body>

{{template "header" .}}

<main class="wrap doc" id="main">
  {{template "contents" .}}
  <article class="prose licences">
    <h1>Licences</h1>
    <p class="doc-lede">The Flockdeck desktop app is free, with its source
       available for noncommercial use. This page gives its licence, then
       every third-party component the desktop app, the phone client and the
       relay are built with, each with its licence and its copyright holder.
       Open <em>Full licence text</em> under any of them to read that licence
       in full.</p>

    <h2 id="flockdeck">The desktop app's licence</h2>
    <p>The Flockdeck desktop app is made by Jim Wright and released under the
       PolyForm Noncommercial licence:</p>
    <pre class="licence"><code>{{.Licences.Own}}</code></pre>
    <p>Its source is on GitHub: <a href="{{.Repo}}">flockdeck</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="desktop">The desktop app</h2>
    <p>Every release of the desktop app carries these notices beside the
       binary, as <code>THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md</code>.</p>
    {{.Licences.Desktop}}

    <h2 id="phone">The phone client</h2>
    <p>The web client you open on a phone, tablet or laptop you have paired.
       It is compiled into the relay, which serves it. It is proprietary:
       © 2026 Jim Wright, all rights reserved. These are the third-party
       components it is built with, each under its own licence.</p>
    {{.Licences.Phone}}
    <h3 id="phone-fonts">The fonts' licence</h3>
    <p>Both typefaces are under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, and
       each comes with its own copy of it, reproduced here.</p>
    {{range .Licences.Fonts}}
    <h4>{{.Name}} — SIL Open Font License 1.1</h4>
    <details class="licence-text"><summary>Full licence text</summary><pre><code>{{.Text}}</code></pre></details>
    {{end}}

    <h2 id="relay">The relay</h2>
    <p>The server that connects your devices to your desktops, as it runs at
       remote.flockdeck.ai. It is proprietary: © 2026 Jim Wright, all rights
       reserved. Its container image carries these notices under
       <code>/licenses</code>.</p>
    {{.Licences.Relay}}

    <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
    <p>flockdeck.ai is set in Archivo and JetBrains Mono, the phone client's
       two typefaces, served from the site itself under the
       <a href="#phone-fonts">SIL Open Font License 1.1</a>. Their licences are
       also beside the fonts, as <a href="fonts/OFL-Archivo.txt">OFL-Archivo.txt</a>
       and <a href="fonts/OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt">OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt</a>.
       Everything else on the site is Flockdeck's own.</p>

    <h2 id="agents">Agents and model APIs</h2>
    <p>Flockdeck starts the agents you choose, such as Claude Code, Codex,
       Gemini CLI, Aider, opencode and Cursor Agent, and talks to the model
       APIs you choose, such as Anthropic's, OpenAI's and Google's. None of
       them is part of Flockdeck or distributed with it. Each keeps its own
       licence and terms, which are between you and whoever provides it; the
       <a href="terms.html#third-party-software-and-services">terms</a> say the
       same.</p>
  </article>
</main>

{{template "footer" .}}
</body>
</html>
